                <pb facs="0161" n="89" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg89"/>

                <head>No. 58.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Trescot to Mr. Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Special Mission of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Lima</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1882-04-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 12, 1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Will leave on the 15th, being absent a few days, to see Montero. I believe bases
                    negotiations between the belligerents can be attained. Is most important I
                    should be in Washington, D. C., before opening of the negotiations to inform you
                    of facts. Telegraph answer Lima.</p>
                <closer><signed>TRESCOT.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
